.TH SPIVariable 2type 2026-08-14 "Linux"

.SH NAME
SPIVariable \- variable representation of piControl driver

.SH LIBRARY
piControl device driver ioctl interface

.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B "#include <piControl.h>"
.sp
.B typedef struct SPIVariableStr {
.BR "    char   strVarName[32];" "  /* Variable name */"
.BR "    __u16  i16uAddress;" "     /* Address of the variable in process image */"
.BR "    __u8   i8uBit;" "          /* which bit position, or whole byte */"
.BR "    __u8   pad;" "             /* padding */"
.BR "    __u16  i16uLength;" "      /* The length of the value */"
.B } SPIVariable;
.fi

.SH DESCRIPTION

.TP
.I strVarName
This field contains the name of the variable.
A variable name can only be up to 32 characters long.
.TP
.I i16uAddress
This field contains the address of the variable in the process image.
.TP
.I i8uBit
This field contains the position of the bit to read if the field
.I i16uLength
is set to
.BR 1 .
.TP
.I pad
This field is padding and must be zeroed.
.TP
.I i16uLength
This field contains the length of the variable. Valid values are
.BR 1 ", " 8 ", " 16 ", and " 32 .
If the value of this field is
.B 1
then the field
.I i8uBit
specifies which bit position contains the value.

.SH SEE ALSO

.BR ioctl (2),
.BR KB_FIND_VARIABLE (2)
